<!-- Phase 9 website teaching layer; original chapter remains read-only. Evidence: website/reviews/android-phase9-findings.md. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The shared screen leaves the navigation stack, but its callback still holds the Swift owner and a Kotlin job still produces state. Sharing an object between threads, keeping it alive, and cancelling its work are three separate questions. Trace the references and the owner before reaching for a GC setting.</p>

