### Follow the owner through the reference graph

<figure class="stepper" data-no-handoff><span class="stepper-title">Why ending a screen is more than dropping one local variable</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="swift"><strong>Swift screen owner</strong><small data-text="swiftV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="kotlin"><strong>Shared state holder</strong><small data-text="kotlinV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="callback"><strong>Registered callback</strong><small data-text="callbackV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Subscribe",
"caption": "The Swift owner retains the shared holder; its registered callback captures the Swift owner in this example.",
"state": {
"swift": "active",
"kotlin": "active",
"callback": "active"
},
"text": {
"swiftV": "retains shared holder",
"kotlinV": "retains callback",
"callbackV": "retains Swift owner"
},
"add": [
"swift",
"kotlin",
"callback"
]
},
{
"label": "Leave screen",
"caption": "Removing a screen from presentation does not by itself identify and break every retained reference.",
"state": {
"swift": "warn"
},
"text": {
"swiftV": "no longer presented; still retained"
}
},
{
"label": "End owned work",
"caption": "At the designed ownership boundary, cancel the observation/work and detach callbacks that are no longer needed.",
"state": {
"callback": "ghost",
"kotlin": "done"
},
"text": {
"callbackV": "registration removed",
"kotlinV": "owned work stopped"
}
},
{
"label": "Verify release",
"caption": "Check the reference graph and runtime memory behaviour. Collection/deinitialization timing depends on the participating runtimes.",
"state": {
"swift": "done"
},
"text": {
"swiftV": "no unwanted ownership path remains"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>This illustrates application ownership, not immediate reclamation or one mandatory Swift bridge API.</figcaption></figure>

